If both your hands are welded to cursed item(s), you can't
get anything into or out of containers, among other problems.
If you're going to use a two-handed weapon or a shield below
the castle (or while quaffing from fountains or doing other
things that create a risk of item crusing), you at minimum
should burn Elbereth somewhere (on a level that isn't very
likely to develop monsters that ignore Elbereth, such as
Minotaurs -- so not in Gehennom) with a wand of fire or
lightning and drop a curse-removal aid on it (e.g., a vial of
holy water or a scroll of remove curse).  Also, it's a really
good idea to have intrinsic teleport control before taking
this risk.

